### Bahi API collection
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or as a reference for curl.
### Set @baseUrl to wherever the API is running.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@customerId = replace-with-a-real-uuid
@itemId = replace-with-a-real-uuid
@invoiceId = replace-with-a-real-uuid

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Customers

### List customers (search / filter / sort all optional)
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers?status=active&sort=total_sales&order=desc&search=

### One customer, with their sales roll-up
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{customerId}}

### Create a customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sharma Traders",
  "email": "accounts@sharmatraders.in",
  "phone": "+91 98300 41125",
  "address": "14/2 Burrabazar, Kolkata, West Bengal 700007",
  "gstin": "19AABCS1429B1Z8",
  "status": "active"
}

### Update a customer (partial update is fine)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "inactive" }

### Delete a customer — 409 if they have invoices
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{customerId}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------- Items

### List items
GET {{baseUrl}}/items?status=active&sort=name&order=asc

### One item
GET {{baseUrl}}/items/{{itemId}}

### Sales history for one item — every invoice line it has appeared on
GET {{baseUrl}}/items/{{itemId}}/invoices

### Create an item
POST {{baseUrl}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Copper Wire 2.5 sq mm — 90 m coil",
  "description": "FR PVC insulated, ISI marked",
  "unit": "coil",
  "unit_price": "3150.00",
  "tax_rate": "18",
  "status": "active"
}

### Update an item
PUT {{baseUrl}}/items/{{itemId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "unit_price": "3299.00" }

### Delete an item — 409 if it appears on any invoice
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/items/{{itemId}}

### ----------------------------------------------------------------- Invoices

### List invoices
GET {{baseUrl}}/invoices?status=all&sort=invoice_date&order=desc

### Only what is still owed, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/invoices?status=partially_paid&sort=amount_pending&order=desc

### Next number in the current financial-year series
GET {{baseUrl}}/invoices/next-number

### One invoice, with its line items and customer details
GET {{baseUrl}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}

### Create an invoice
### Amounts are never sent by the client: quantities, prices and rates are,
### and the server computes every total.
POST {{baseUrl}}/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invoice_number": null,
  "customer_id": "{{customerId}}",
  "invoice_date": "2026-09-11",
  "notes": "Delivery by 20 September.",
  "amount_paid": "0",
  "items": [
    { "item_id": "{{itemId}}", "quantity": "40" },
    { "item_id": "{{itemId}}", "quantity": "2.5", "unit_price": "3000.00", "tax_rate": "12" }
  ]
}

### Replace an invoice (lines are replaced wholesale, totals recalculated)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invoice_number": "INV-2026-27-0001",
  "customer_id": "{{customerId}}",
  "invoice_date": "2026-09-11",
  "amount_paid": "50000",
  "items": [{ "item_id": "{{itemId}}", "quantity": "10" }]
}

### Record a payment — absolute amount received so far, not a delta
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/payment
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount_paid": "125000.00" }

### Mark an invoice paid in full
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/payment
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mark_as": "paid" }

### Delete an invoice
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}

### ------------------------------------------------------ Dashboard & reports

### Everything the dashboard needs, in one request
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard

### Customer-wise sales
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/customer-sales

### Item-wise sales
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/item-sales

### Pending payments
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/pending-payments
